## Setting Up Your Phone as a Chromecast Remote

### Requirements

- Chromecast with Google TV (HD or 4K)
- Android phone on the **same Wi-Fi network** as the Chromecast
- TV Remote for Android TV app installed on your phone

### Pairing Steps

**Step 1:** Power on your Chromecast with Google TV and let it reach the home screen.

**Step 2:** On your Android phone, make sure you're on the same Wi-Fi network as the Chromecast. Go to Settings → Wi-Fi and confirm the network name matches.

**Step 3:** Open **TV Remote for Android TV** ([available on the Play Store](https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.hari.androidtvremote)). The app will immediately begin scanning for compatible devices on your network.

**Step 4:** Your Chromecast with Google TV will appear in the device list, typically labeled by the name you gave it during setup (e.g., "Living Room Chromecast"). Tap it.

**Step 5:** A 6-digit PIN will appear on your TV screen. Enter this PIN in the app and tap **Pair**. The connection is now saved.

You're done. From this point on, opening the app will automatically reconnect to your Chromecast.

