## D-Pad Navigation on Chromecast with Google TV

The D-pad (directional pad) is the primary way to navigate Google TV's interface. It's a focus-based system — a visible highlight moves between UI elements as you press directional buttons, and you press the center button to select.

### Core D-Pad Controls

| Button | Action |
|---|---|
| Up / Down / Left / Right | Move focus between cards, apps, and buttons |
| Center (OK/Select) | Confirm selection / open item |
| Back | Go to previous screen |
| Home | Return to Google TV home screen |
| Long-press Home | Open Google Assistant |
| Long-press Back | Open quick settings on some builds |

### Navigating the Google TV Home Screen

The Google TV home screen is organized into tabs:
- **For You** — Personalized content recommendations
- **Movies**, **Shows**, **Apps**, **Library** — Category tabs

Use Left/Right to move between tabs at the top. Use Up/Down to move between content rows within a tab. Press the center button to open a movie or app. These are the same actions whether you use the physical remote or a phone app.

