## Using the Keyboard for Google Search on Chromecast

One of the biggest quality-of-life improvements a phone remote offers over the physical Chromecast remote is **keyboard input**. The physical remote has a voice button, but if you prefer typing — for passwords, usernames, or quiet situations — navigating Google TV's on-screen keyboard with D-pad is tedious.

With the TV Remote app:
1. When your Chromecast displays an on-screen keyboard (e.g., in YouTube's search bar), tap the **keyboard icon** in the app
2. Your phone's keyboard opens
3. Type normally — characters appear on the TV screen in real time

This works in every app that uses a standard Android text field: YouTube search, Netflix search, Google Play Store login, web browsers, and more. The latency is near-zero because the text is sent over your local network.

