## What to Do If You Lose the Chromecast Physical Remote

Lost your Chromecast remote? It happens. Here's what you can do:

### Option 1: Use a Phone App (Best Solution)

Install **TV Remote for Android TV** on your Android phone. As long as your Chromecast is powered on and both devices are on the same Wi-Fi network, you'll have full control within minutes. This is the easiest solution and arguably better than the physical remote because of the keyboard.

### Option 2: Use the Google TV App

Google's official Google TV app (on both Android and iOS) includes a built-in remote feature. It works similarly to third-party apps but requires a Google account sign-in.

### Option 3: Buy a Replacement Remote

Google sells replacement Chromecast remotes on the Google Store. Third-party universal remotes with HDMI-CEC support may also work, depending on your TV model.

### Option 4: HDMI-CEC via Your TV Remote

If your TV supports HDMI-CEC (sometimes branded as AnyNet+, Bravia Sync, Simplink, etc.), you may be able to control your Chromecast using your TV's physical remote via the HDMI connection. Enable HDMI-CEC in your TV's settings and see if D-pad commands pass through.

